\caption(The computed query distance is five, with squared distance 25 and original witness (0,0). Dashed axis-aligned legs distinguish the Euclidean segment from a seven-step grid route.)
\alttext(An equal-scale right triangle has horizontal leg four, vertical leg three and a blue site-to-query segment labelled distance five.)

> Derive the one-dimensional envelope

For finite sample costs f(p), allow positive infinity to mean no candidate.
At each integer q, compute

\[
D(q)=\min_p\{f(p)+(q-p)^2\}.
\]

Every finite p supplies a parabola of the same curvature. Equating the
parabolas at p<q and cancelling the shared squared query term gives their
crossing

\[
s(p,q)=\frac{(f(q)+q^2)-(f(p)+p^2)}{2(q-p)}
=\frac{p+q}{2}+\frac{f(q)-f(p)}{2(q-p)}.
\]

The implementation uses the factored expression with long-double operands,
dividing costs before subtraction. It never multiplies signed integer
indices. Positive-infinity candidates are skipped, avoiding infinity-minus-
infinity arithmetic and the former finite placeholder of 1e20.
NaN and negative-infinity costs are rejected; finite negative costs are
valid for this generalized minimum-cost transform. They need not describe
squared distances and are not square-rooted by the one-dimensional API.

Keep increasing candidate indices and increasing left boundaries. If a
new crossing lies at or before the last candidate’s boundary, remove that
candidate and compare again. Otherwise append the new candidate. During
evaluation, advance the winner pointer only after the next boundary is
strictly smaller than the integer query. An exact boundary tie therefore
keeps the smaller source index.

Take f=(0,infinity,9,infinity,0). Candidate 2 first enters at 13/4=3.25.
Candidate 4 crosses it at 3/4=0.75, before that left boundary, so candidate
2 is removed. Comparing 4 against 0 gives crossing two. The final envelope
uses candidates [0,4], and q=2 selects candidate 0 at the exact tie.
The table exposes the actual comparisons from that execution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/edt_envelope.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const double inf=std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  const auto t=dm::geometry::squared_distance_transform_1d_trace({0,inf,9,inf,0});
  std::print("Final candidates {}; values {}; selected indices {}.\n\n",t.envelope_sites,t.values,t.nearest_index);
  std::print("| new candidate | previous candidate | crossing | previous left boundary | removed previous |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& e:t.comparisons)std::print("| {} | {} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} | {} |\n",e.candidate,e.previous,e.intersection,e.previous_begin,e.removed);
  std::print("\nActual work: {} samples, {} finite candidates, {} intersections, {} pushes, {} pops, {} winner advances, {} evaluations.\n",t.work.input_values,t.work.finite_candidates,t.work.intersections,t.work.envelope_pushes,t.work.envelope_pops,t.work.selection_advances,t.work.evaluations);
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37,99,235},{220,38,38},{22,163,74}};
  std::size_t series=0;for(std::size_t p:{0u,2u,4u}){std::vector<double> x,y;
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<=160;++i){const double q=i/40.0;x.push_back(q);y.push_back(t.costs[p]+(q-p)*(q-p));}
    plot.line(x,y,std::format("candidate {}",p),colors[series++]);}
  plot.points({0,1,2,3,4},t.values,"sampled min",{0,0,0},6)
   .title("Actual envelope discards candidate 2").x_label("query location").y_label("generalized squared cost")
   .y_limits(-.5,24).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/edt_envelope.svg");
}
```
